# Henry coefficient of CO2 by Widom test-particle insertion in the empty rigid framework
# -- generated by scripts/make_inputs.py. Same force field, charges, Ewald and T as the isotherm.
# K_H = beta/rho_f * <exp(-beta U_insert)> (RASPA prints it in mol/kg/Pa); independent of any isotherm fit.
SimulationType                MonteCarlo
NumberOfCycles                {cycles}
NumberOfInitializationCycles  0
PrintEvery                    5000
RestartFile                   no

Forcefield                    local
CutOffVDW                     {cutoff}
ChargeMethod                  Ewald
CutOffChargeCharge            {cutoff}
EwaldPrecision                1e-6
UseChargesFromCIFFile         yes

Framework 0
FrameworkName                 {framework}
RemoveAtomNumberCodeFromLabel yes
UnitCells                     {unit_cells}
ExternalTemperature           {temperature}

Component 0 MoleculeName             CO2
            MoleculeDefinition       local
            WidomProbability         1.0
            CreateNumberOfMolecules  0
